model URealPairwise

-- Authored specifically to give unc-modelvalidator's general uncertain-vs-uncertain
-- ordered comparison (UReal vs UReal over MULTI-CANDIDATE value and uncertainty
-- domains) a real, wired benchmark scenario. The proven-equal-singleton slice
-- refused every configuration where the two sides' uncertainties were not the
-- same singleton constant; the pairwise enumeration evaluates each candidate
-- pair with USE'S OWN evaluator classes (bit-exact, crossing-point model
-- included) and admits exactly the pairs whose probability clears theta.
--
-- The discriminating shape: A's uncertainty candidates {0.0, 0.05} straddle
-- theta = 0.999. With u_A = 0.05 the equal-sigma crossing model gives
-- P(A < B) ~ 0.9973 (below theta); with u_A = 0.0 the degenerate branch gives
-- P = 1 - CNDF(-6) ~ 1.0 (above it). So exactly one candidate pair satisfies,
-- and a correct encoding must force the witness to carry u_A = 0.0.

class Sensor
attributes
  speedA : UReal
  speedB : UReal
end

constraints

context s : Sensor inv aBelowBTight:
  (s.speedA < s.speedB).toBooleanC(0.999)
